WEBVTT

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.520
I'm joining the rhythmic gymnastics club!

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.700
Really? You are?!

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.280
That was one great backflip!

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.030
Incredible! On your first day, no less!

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.580
Outta sight! Seriously outta sight!

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.980
I knew you had what it takes!

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.170
You've got a real knack!
You're a prodigy!

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.450
Actually, anyone can do that 
once they know how.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.700
In fact, it's the easiest move 
in all rhythmic gym—

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.550
Silence, Super Ace!

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.920
We can't let this one get away.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:36.510
<b>Shotaro  Futaba</b>

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.280
Heck yeah! We got our sixth!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.730
Club Application

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.730
April 8th, 2022

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.730
Class 1-B, Student no. 27\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hShotaro Futaba

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.730
I have completed the necessary procedures to join the <u>Men's Rhythmic Gymnastics</u> club.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.730
Advisor's name

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.730
Stamp

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.500
Hey, so the "Sho" in your name 
is the character for "Soar," huh?

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.080
I like it! Perfect for a rhythmic gymnast.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.770
Welcome to the club, Shotaro.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.570
Th-Thank you for having me!

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.110
Misato-kun!

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.450
Thank you!

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.300
I managed to do it because 
I mimicked your backflips.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.370
Wait, it wasn't because 
of my great instruction?

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.180
About your instruction, Shichigahama...

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.550
Yeah, about your instruction...

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.640
It makes no sense! I'm so sorry!

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.110
I didn't do anything special.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.380
Even so, thank you!

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.890
Let's see... I think
 it's about time for this.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.520
Teamwork is important 
in men's rhythmic gymnastics.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.640
So the boys live in a dorm together.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.470
How would you two feel about that?

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.700
Living in a dorm?

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.690
Sorry. I really need 
to go home in the evenings.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.090
Oh, yeah?

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.020
Well, everyone's family
 situation is different.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.320
I'm sorry.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.340
As for you, Futaba-kun,
talk to your parents about it.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.740
Yes, sir!

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:13.960
<b><i>Backflip!!</i></b>

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.750
Wow! Awesome!

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.420
See the Facility

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.550
What is it, Ayu-chan?

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.620
The homepage has pictures 
of the dorm where he'll be staying!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.490
Soushukan High School's baseball team 
is a regular at Koshien Stadium,

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.850
and its soccer team 
is a regular at nationals.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.440
I hear they have athletes 
from all over the country.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.570
And the men's rhythmic gymnastics 
team gets to stay there, too?

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:37.940
Yeah, looks like.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.510
My, they must have high hopes.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.920
<b>SENDAI STATION</b>

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.170
<b>Track 5 Departures</b>

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.170
<b>Track 6 Departures</b>

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.170
<b>Local\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFukushima

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.170
<b>Local\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hShiraishi

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.020
<b>Train arriving</b>

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.670
<b>Track 6 Departures</b>

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.670
<b>Local</b>

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.670
<b>Iwanuma</b>

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:00.440
<i>An inbound train
 is arriving on track 3.</i>

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.270
<b>Train arriving</b>

00:03:58.690 --> 00:03:59.570
<b>Train arriving</b>

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.300
<i>For your safety, please stay 
behind the yellow line.</i>

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.110
First up, we need to decide 
on a class representative.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.400
Class Representative

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.400
1st Period

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.540
Raise your hand if you're interested.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.960
What? No takers?

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.080
Okay, then...

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.530
<b>Men's Rhythmic
Gymnastics Club</b>

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:28.530
Okay!

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.500
I-I'm coming in!

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.500
Hello.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.010
Hey.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.500
Oh, hello!

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:37.310
You made it, eh?

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.880
Watari, you're scaring him.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.790
Shotaro, that bag...

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.630
Did your parents give their blessing?

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.240
Y-Yes!

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.640
I'll be staying with you guys.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.290
We'll be working together too, Misato-kun.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.090
Yeah.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.940
Misato-kun, what class are you?

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:54.920
Class B.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.160
Oh, yeah? I'm in Class C.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.020
I wish we could've been together...

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.190
Heya!

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.080
Hey!

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.080
Hi.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:01.700
Hello.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:02.420
H-Hello!

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.840
Hey, Misato, Shotaro! You made it.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.580
We're going on a field trip today.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.290
Meet up in front of the school gate!

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.210
Right!

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.670
Field trip?

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.810
Are we jogging?

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.420
You'd better keep up,

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.040
Former Ace! Brief!

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.430
"Former Ace"?

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:17.420
"Brief"?

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.260
Misato may have been an ace
 back in middle school.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.770
But I'm the ace on <i>this</i> team!

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.990
And Shotaro's last name is "Futaba,"

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.080
as in "Brothers" and  "Leaf," 
so "Brief" for short.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.220
Whaddya think?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.210
I hate it.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.620
I would also kind of... 
prefer something else.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.480
What, why?!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.230
One, two! One, two!

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:44.110
We rent out Sekiou University's gymnasium 
for an hour twice every week.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.890
Why the university gym?

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:47.780
You'll understand when you see it.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.280
<b>Sekiou University</b>

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.280
Hey, hey...

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.660
Yeah!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.880
<b>Precepts for Life

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.880
<b>Success without effort leads to arrogance.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.760
It's a men's rhythmic gymnastics mat.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.750
We came here to use this?

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:44.880
But why don't we have one at our school?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.010
That mat costs 15 million yen.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.890
Okay, let's start practice!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.060
<b>Drive  Dedication  Courage!!</b>

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.050
Huh?

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:03.510
I know that flashy tumbling 
and throws are what get attention,

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:06.900
but these freehand exercises 
are actually a lot more important.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.330
Freehand exercises?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.720
Movements you do without an 
apparatus. Like calisthenics.

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:14.900
Captain Shichigahama 
is the team's specialist

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:19.370
in making these freehand exercises 
look grand and impressive.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:22.080
Balance, flexibility...

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.040
Those are Onagawa-senpai's specialties.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.090
His flexibility is exceptional.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:32.470
Watari-kun is the best at handstand holds.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:38.710
Freehand exercises, tumbling, 
and lifts come together

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:41.940
to create a full men's 
rhythmic gymnastics routine.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:43.900
Good summary.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:47.570
Um, what's your specialty, Tsukidate-senpai?

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:50.230
Tsukidate-senpai is an all-rounder.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:53.310
So he can do everything?! That's amazing!

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:56.320
Okay, enough talk. Let's get to practicing.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:57.870
Right!

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.390
P-Pretty good, I guess...

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.840
Seriously. Can't help but wonder 
why he's here of all places.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.090
Onagawa...

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.930
Okay, one more time!

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.810
<b>Men's
Rhythmic
Gymnastics
Club</b>

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:25.980
Good work today.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:26.630
So long!

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.730
See ya tomorrow, Newbie Ace!

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.880
Don't call me "Newbie Ace."

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.310
We'd better head home, too.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:35.400
We'll escort you to the dorm, Futaba-kun!

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:36.540
Yes!

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.780
I'd appreciate it.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:39.280
This way!

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:40.450
Okay!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.910
Keep up.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:43.770
Okay!

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.130
See the Facility

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.070
<b>Sports Dorm</b>

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.290
Wait... huh?

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.550
S-Senpai?

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.490
Keep walking.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.780
U-Um...

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.770
Just keep walking!

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:07.060
Here?

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:11.620
Yep! This is the men's 
rhythmic gymnastics club dorm.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:15.230
It used to house the 
baseball and soccer teams.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:15.900
<b>Men's Rhythmic
Gymnastics Club Dorm</b>

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:17.350
Then it turned into a storage facility,

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:21.160
but our coach talked to the principal
 so we could use it.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.250
This one right here is yours.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.330
<b>Battles Without 
Morals 
and Humanity</b>

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.330
<b>Truck Dad
{*}</b>

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.540
<b>Jingi</b>

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.540
<b>Ninkyo</b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b>Truck Dad (1)</b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b>Truck Dad (2)</b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b>TURF
WARS</b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b><i>Battles Without Morals and Humanity [The Bloody Battle]</i></b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b><i>Battles Without Morals and Humanity [Koganei Never Sleeps)]</i></b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b><i>Life 
on the
 Edge</i></b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b>Like a She-Devil</b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b><i>Daigokudo</i></b>

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.370
<b>The Youxia of Japan</b>

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.390
You're roomin' with Watari!

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.820
Look after Shotaro, will ya, Watari?

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:32.630
Yah.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.800
You heard the man.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.260
Welcome, roomie.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.260
A p-pleasure...

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.270
You're scaring him, Watari.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.730
Well, let's have dinner.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.320
Watari-senpai, you're so good at that!

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.820
My folks run a ramen place, is all.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.480
My family runs a fish market!

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:00.950
<b>FISH</b>

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:00.950
<b>BIG</b>

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:00.950
Tonight's curry is on my dad.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:03.910
My family makes sasa kamaboko!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.080
In business for 110 years!

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:08.460
This is Sasashichi's
 mild sasakama! It's great!

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.460
110 Years in Business

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.460
<b>Sasa 
Kamaboko</b>

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.460
<b>Plain</b>

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.690
Sasakama?

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.270
My family runs a shrine.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.300
If you ever have sleep paralysis,
you can come to us.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:17.420
<b>Kumano Shrine 

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.540
I don't think that's the right kind...

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:21.110
Shotaro, your family's in Sendai, right?

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.870
What do your parents do?

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:27.180
My dad works for the city office, 
doing stuff with the burial mounds.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.360
My mom's a housewife, and I have a little 
sister in her second year of middle school.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.810
Is she cute?

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:34.650
Onagawa.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.110
Just kidding, sheesh.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.570
Don't worry. I have Ma-chan—

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.570
Say, Onagawa.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:43.410
I feel like we're not quite in sync on the
 salto layouts at the end of our group start.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:48.180
That's our captain. 
You picked up on that, did you?

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:51.360
Yeah, it's just not working out...

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.170
I noticed.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:55.460
Maybe you're trying too hard 
to match our timing?

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.800
It's not goin' great for me, either.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.370
For real...

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:01.200
<i>It starts today...</i>

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:01.800
It's been a weakness of mine, 
so I get in my head.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.980
I keep telling you, we'll match you... 
Just go like <i>vwoosh</i>!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.690
<i>My new daily life!</i>

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:05.690
"Vwoosh"?

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:06.600
Yeah, <i>vwoosh</i>.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:21.990
Watari-senpai? It's morning...

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.180
G'won an' kill me...

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.730
How's Futaba-kun looking, Asa-chan?

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:32.850
He's been here a week. He learns quickly.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.960
Though he's nowhere near ready yet.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:41.370
All right.

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:44.150
Now that we have a full team of six,

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:46.810
I'd like to do the routine 
this year with everybody.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.430
What's the routine?

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:52.740
Last year's was originally 
choreographed for six,

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:52.740
I get to perform with them?

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:56.190
but since we didn't have enough people, 
we reworked it for four.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:59.310
So now we can do it 
how it was meant to be done.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:02.410
But before we start practice... Futaba-kun.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:04.070
Yes?

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.460
Go from one end of the mat 
to the other. Backflips only.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.380
Y-Yes, sir!

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.040
Ow...

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.050
We'll have a test in one week.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:23.840
I want you to be able to do 
the full backflip run by then.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:28.660
If you can't, we'll do this year's 
routine with a team of five.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:29.350
Huh?!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:30.220
Coach!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.360
The prefectural tournament 
is at the end of May.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:33.830
We don't have much time.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:38.100
Putting him on the mat when he 
can't keep up would be dangerous.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.610
"Nothing good comes of forcing oneself."

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.860
That's what my wife always says.

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.080
Wh-What's wrong?

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.070
The coach loves his wife 
and talks about her constantly...

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.870
But none of us have ever met her.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.750
We think he just made her up.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.350
Isn't that right, Asa-chan?

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:00.300
Yeah, she says that.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.300
He made her up?

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:07.000
By the way, the manager is the coach's wife's 
little sister's husband's big sister's daughter.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.830
So they're related?

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:13.080
Of course, you can opt not to take the test.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:14.660
What'll it be, Futaba-kun?

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.750
I'll do it!

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:25.580
Then I want you to be in charge 
of Futaba-kun's training, Misato-kun.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:27.450
Wh-Why me?

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:30.710
Ah, you'd better be off 
or you'll be late to class.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:32.970
Dismissed for now. Good work today.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:34.430
Thank you!

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.820
One week...

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.340
Let's do it, Misato-kun!

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:49.010
Sheesh. You think Shotaro'll make it?

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.970
I wonder why the coach put 
Misato in charge of training him.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.340
One more time.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:54.510
O-Okay.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:01.530
You're going limp in the knees.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:03.590
Make sure they don't come too far forward.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.020
R-Right...

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.830
That's all for today. Good work.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.120
Thank you!

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.490
Misato-kun, can we try a little longer?

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:15.840
You know the basics.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:18.110
Just have to keep doing it
until you get it right.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:19.070
I'm off.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:21.430
S-Sure... Good work.

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:23.460
Th-Thank you! Good work today!

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.470
What cool customer... 
That's our Frozen Ace.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.400
It's hot! So hot!

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.400
Thank you as always!

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.560
They're best like that.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.590
Takoyaki skewers?

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:38.720
Yeah. A local specialty.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.880
Still great!

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:43.100
Go on! Eat up!

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:46.100
You don't want to lose to the Frozen Ace!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.900
Futaba. Wake up.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:54.980
Futaba!

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.290
Misato-kun?!

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:03.650
Is it a raid?!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:08.310
Let's go.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:09.780
O-Okay...

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.300
Misato came by?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.830
Said he can't be here at night, 
but mornings're A-okay.

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.140
Can't tell if he's as cool 
as a cucumber or burning up.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.060
But he just walked in?

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.300
Who was in charge of locking up last night?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.270
I'm so sorry!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.500
<b><i>Test!!</i></b>

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:41.970
Okay!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:52.140
<i>I managed to do it because 
I mimicked your backflips.</i>

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.780
Misato-kun?

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.210
<i>If I could soar like that,</i>

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:22.830
<i>I know I'd see the world differently.</i>

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:32.160
Let's get started.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:32.970
Come on.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:35.340
Yeah!

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:38.240
Shotaro, uh...

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:42.360
What's he up to?

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.370
Ah, jeez!

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:55.930
Another day of failure!

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:57.490
I have to go now.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.680
Good work today.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.780
You're leaving?!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:02.770
Hey, the test is tomorrow!

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:03.500
Hey!

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:05.000
Misato!

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:06.880
Sorry.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.170
What's with that guy?

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:14.240
Coach, do you mind if 
we practice a little more?

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.740
That's fine, but...

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:18.680
Remember that we don't have
 the gym for much longer.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.840
<i>The train will arrive shortly.</i>

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:28.660
<i>For your safety, please stay 
behind the yellow line.</i>

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:35.200
Now you can practice as long as you'd like.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.520
Th-This is...

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:40.260
Well, it's just normal mats over cardboard...

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.200
Thank you so much!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.920
Just don't push yourself too hard.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:51.450
It's <i>our</i> dream to have a full team
at the Inter-High, not yours.

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:55.280
Yeah. And you only just started 
doing rhythmic gymnastics...

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.480
It might not be possible this year, 
but there's always next year—

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:59.590
No, there's not!

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:05.240
Because... you'll have graduated by then.

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:08.990
This is the only year I'll be able
 to perform with all of you.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:14.940
A-And seeing your backflips 
is what brought me to Ao High.

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:18.990
I admire you all so much, and I...

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.120
I want...

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:23.360
I want to soar with you!

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.340
Shotaro...

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.510
I'm flattered, but...

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:33.340
How does a guy just come out and say—

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:36.090
Y-You cryin'?

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.010
Of course not!

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:41.870
We're the same way, Shotaro.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:46.790
When I was in junior high, 
I couldn't go to school.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:48.710
I was adrift.

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:49.690
That's when...

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:57.420
He taught me how to do a backflip,

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:59.740
then about rhythmic gymnastics.

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:03.450
Me and Onagawa joined in soon after.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:05.320
We've kind of been 
a group since kindergarten.

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:07.240
We got worried and came to check in on him,

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.320
and so we discovered
this cool thing he was doing.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.670
Same here.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:15.920
I joined Ao High, and their backflips...
 w-were electrifying.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:22.640
I guess we all started rhythmic 
gymnastics to do backflips.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.440
So we're just like you.

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:26.760
No kidding.

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:28.800
I can't believe what a bunch of simple—

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:29.640
Why aren't you people working?

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:30.920
Misato-kun!

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:33.430
I thought you went home!

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:35.270
I made sure it was okay.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.440
But I still want to get home 
as soon as possible.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:38.980
We don't have much time.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:40.670
Nail this, Futaba.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:42.220
Right!

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:55.100
<i>So we're just like you.</i>

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.100
<i>With my senpais...</i>

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.740
<i>With Misato-kun...</i>

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:25.990
<i>I want to soar with you!</i>

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.420
You pass.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:42.760
Yes!

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:43.300
Shotaro!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:44.510
Yahoo!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:44.510
Hey—

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:51.430
I think Misato-kun performed so it was
easier for Futaba-kun to understand.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.190
Though it's still impressive 
that Futaba-kun pulled it off.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:56.230
Great job, Grief!

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.230
"Grief"?

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.960
"Great job, Leaf!" Or "Grief" for short!

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.960
I would still kind of... 
prefer something else.

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:03.860
Right, Surprisingly Passionate Ace?

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.240
Don't call me "Surprisingly Passionate Ace."

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:08.700
It wasn't bad.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.750
Yeah, I know I still have a long way to go.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.620
But thank you, Misato-kun!

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:20.500
I swear I'll catch up to you!
